issue_body:
If you want to display product availability in the cart, and show availability_message, it returns the wrong text. Like it always has the in-stock product, it doesn't show the message for available_later text. My client had products where the stock was 0. But in the cart, it displays an "in stock" label.

I tried it in PS 1.7.6.2 version. 
Long story short :D 
src/Adapter/Presenter/Product/ProductLazyArray.php:773 line always gets $product['quantity'] more than 0. In Cart class applyProductCalculations() method is clearly visible, that $product['quantity'] is overwriten by cart_quantity. 

`    protected function applyProductCalculations($row, $shopContext, $productQuantity = null)
    {
        if (null === $productQuantity) {
            $productQuantity = (int) $row['cart_quantity'];
        }

        if (isset($row['ecotax_attr']) && $row['ecotax_attr'] > 0) {
            $row['ecotax'] = (float) $row['ecotax_attr'];
        }

        $row['stock_quantity'] = (int) $row['quantity'];
        // for compatibility with 1.2 themes
        $row['quantity'] = $productQuantity;`
So in ProductLazyArray.php we need to take **stock_quantity instead** of **quantity**

#### Expected behavior
In cart show product availability when out of stock with the allowed order option. like _Delivery in 10-15days.

#### Steps to Reproduce

add product with 0 quantity, select Allow orders. 
Set Label when out of stock.
Add 
```
    {block name='product_availability'}
      <span id="product-availability">
        {if $product.show_availability && $product.availability_message}
          {if $product.availability == 'available'}
            <i class="material-icons rtl-no-flip product-available">&#xE5CA;</i>
          {elseif $product.availability == 'last_remaining_items'}
            <i class="material-icons product-last-items">&#xE002;</i>
          {else}
            <i class="material-icons product-unavailable">&#xE14B;</i>
          {/if}
          {$product.availability_message}
        {/if}
      </span>
    {/block}
``` 
in `templates/checkout/_partials/cart-detailed-product-line.tpl`

#### Additional information

* PrestaShop version: 1.7.6.2
* PHP version: 7.2

When requesting a category from Web service, the "position" field is returned with a wrong value, so if you use this returned category and change eg. its name and post it back to the web service, the category's position changes.

Steps to reproduce:
1. Do a GET curl request to eg. (will return category "clothes" from demo presta store data)
   prestapi/api/categories/3
2. Check database ps_category for id 3 the position is 0.
2. Position returned in response is 5 instead of 0:

```xml
<position>
   <![CDATA[5]]>
</position>
```

Optionally you can also try to update:
1. Update category with:

```php

<html><head><title>CRUD Tutorial - Create example</title></head><body>
<?php
require_once("vendor/autoload.php");

define('DEBUG', true);
ini_set('display_errors','on');
define('PS_SHOP_PATH', 'http://localhost/presta176');
define('PS_WS_AUTH_KEY', 'the key goes here');
require_once('PSWebServiceLibrary.php');
$webService= new PrestaShopWebservice(PS_SHOP_PATH, PS_WS_AUTH_KEY, DEBUG);

$category_id = 3;

//
// Get existing categpry
//
$xml = $webService->get(array('resource' => 'categories', 'id' => $category_id));

//
// Get blank schema
//
$category = $xml->children()->children();

$category->name->language[0][0] = "New name";
unset($category->level_depth);
unset($category->nb_products_recursive);
unset($category->associations);

$opt['putXml'] = $xml->asXML();                  
$opt['id'] = $category_id;
$opt['resource'] = 'categories';
$xml = $webService->edit($opt);
echo "DONE";
```
2. Check category and it is now gone to the bottom because getting the existing category returned wrong position 5 instead of 0.


Now the position is 5, and if you try getting it again it will return again, wrong number, 6.
